[size=6][b]The Longest Year[/b][/size]
[size=4][b]Restore the Community Center within a single year — or the Junimos rewind the seasons and you begin again, a little stronger.[/b][/size]

A roguelite time-loop for Stardew Valley (PC).

[b]The Longest Year[/b] turns Stardew Valley's first year into a roguelite loop. Each season asks you to give back enough of the land's bounty to the old Community Center hall. Fall short by a season's end and the Junimos turn time back to Spring 1 — the world resets, but the strength you've earned (and the power your offerings bank) can carry forward. Restore the whole Center inside one year to break the loop for good.

[color=yellow]This is a [b]beta[/b] (0.18.58). It is feature-complete for v1 and stable in testing; what it most needs now is feedback on [b]difficulty, pricing, and pacing[/b]. See Giving feedback below.[/color]

[color=yellow][b]This is the last big engine update.[/b] From here the plan is bug fixes and balance passes driven by your feedback, and then work begins on the story. So this is the version to tell me what is wrong with.[/color]

[line]

[size=5][b]See it played[/b][/size]

[b]Emmalution[/b] is playing the whole loop on YouTube, and her edited episodes are the best introduction to the mod there is. Thank you, Emma, for the videos and for the bug reports that came with them.

[list]
[*][b]Spring:[/b] [url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fU4EVzlD1K8]I must donate to the Community Centre OR RESET![/url]
[*][b]Summer:[/b] [url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WaAzDjMWmt8]The Junimos challenged me to complete these bundles...[/url]
[/list]
Channel: [url=https://www.youtube.com/@emmalution]youtube.com/@emmalution[/url]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.65[/b][/size]

[b]Keep your favourite barn and coop animals through a rewind with the new Herd Book, and the Start with an animal keeps can finally be bought.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]The Herd Book.[/b] A new book you carry from the first day, like the Cookbook and Craftbook. Put an animal in one of its slots and it comes back after every rewind as the same animal: same name, same hearts, fully grown. You start with one Chicken slot. Junimo Upgrades sells the rest in a fixed order: a second Chicken, then two each for Cows, Ducks, Goats, Rabbits, Sheep and Pigs, then one each for the Void Chicken, Golden Chicken, Dinosaur and Ostrich. Suggested by tanky24u.
[*][b]It needs a home to come back to.[/b] An animal returns only when you keep a building it can live in and there is room inside. Otherwise it waits in the book and tries again next loop, and the book tells you which keep a slot needs.
[*][b]The Herd Book opens before a rewind.[/b] After the Cookbook and Craftbook, it opens on its own when it has an empty slot and an animal on your farm that fits it.
[*][b]Start with an animal can be bought.[/b] None of the ten Start with keeps could ever be bought, because the mod never noticed the animals you owned. It now notes every kind of animal on your farm each morning, so once you have had a chicken, Start with Chicken is for sale after Keep Coop.
[*][b]Start with Ostrich uses a Barn.[/b] Ostriches live in barns, but this keep put one in a Deluxe Coop. It now needs Keep Barn.
[*][b]A full building stays full.[/b] A Start with animal no longer squeezes into a coop or barn that has no room.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.58[/b][/size]

[b]Start the year over whenever you like from the Junimo Shrine, and season pity is gone.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Restart the year.[/b] The Junimo Shrine on your farm has a new Restart the year button. It works like a failed season without the Junimo scene: the day ends right away, you choose whether to keep your bundles, spend JP in Junimo Upgrades, bank recipes, and wake on Spring 1 of the next loop. Your JP carries over as usual, and a restart counts as a loop, so holding the same board again still costs more each time in a row. The button is hidden on the last day of a season and while an event or festival is playing. Suggested by tanky24u.
[*][b]It works after Keep playing too.[/b] If you won and kept playing, a restart starts a fresh loop that can be won again.
[*][b]The Junimos no longer offer to ease a season you keep failing.[/b] A Fail night now asks one thing, whether to keep your bundles or let them reshuffle, and then opens the upgrade menu. If a season is too hard, turn it down with the Difficulty settings instead. A season the Junimos had already eased goes back to normal. The "Hold and pity prices" setting is now just "Hold prices".
[*][b]Fortune: Rare Fish's description now says what it does.[/b] The upgrade menu used to say "Rare fish catch chance increased by 25%", which is not how it works. It now reads "Your rod always works as if it has a Curiosity Lure." Reported by tanky24u.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.50[/b][/size]

[b]Missed a fish or forage item in its season? Buy the season back for a week.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Spring Returns, Summer Returns and Fall Returns.[/b] Three new one-week boosts at the Junimo Shrine, 100 JP each. Each is sold once its season has passed this loop: Spring Returns from Summer on, Summer Returns from Fall on, Fall Returns in Winter. While one runs, that season's fish bite and its forage turns up again, on top of the current season's. Time of day, weather and fishing spots still apply, and the legendary fish are included, still once per loop.
[*][b]Seasonal items are back on their normal deadlines.[/b] 0.18.47 made a seasonal fish or forage item due by the last season it could be found. The Returns boosts replace that: a Summer-only fish can be due at Winter again, and if you missed it, Summer Returns brings it back. Reported by tanky24u.
[*][b]Rain Dance works in Winter.[/b] A past season's rain fish can be caught in Winter with Rain Dance and a Returns boost. Snow still does not count as rain. Storm Call is still not sold in Winter.
[*][b]Two descriptions swapped a line.[/b] 0.18.47 took Artichoke out of the wrong description. Year-Two Seeds now lists only Garlic and Red Cabbage, and Pierre's year-2 seeds upgrade lists Artichoke again, which he does stock.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.47[/b][/size]

[b]Boosted crops look ready when they are, seasonal items stop being due after they leave, and the rewind's upgrade menu gets its own name.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Crops sped up by a boost look ready when they are ready.[/b] Growth Spurt, the Farming week bonus and Green Thumb added their extra day after the game's own nightly growth, so a crop they finished could be picked while it still looked half grown. Wild seeds were hit hardest, because they never turned into their forage. The extra day now comes first. Green Thumb also no longer makes a ready regrowing crop look unripe for a day. Reported by tanky24u.
[*][b]A seasonal item is never due after its season ends.[/b] A Summer-only fish like the Pufferfish could be due by Winter, so Summer and Fall let you through without it and the loop then failed at Winter, when it could no longer be caught. Every item is now due by the last season it can be found, so a missing Pufferfish shows up at the end of Summer instead of two seasons later. Reported by tanky24u.
[*][b]Year-Two Seeds is Spring and Summer only.[/b] Fall Mixed Seeds already grow Artichoke a quarter of the time, so the Fall version only nudged that to about 29%. It can no longer be bought in Fall. Raised by tanky24u.
[*][b]The upgrade menu has its own name.[/b] The menu where you spend JP on keeps after a rewind is now called Junimo Upgrades, and the Shrine prices setting is now Upgrade prices. The Junimo Shrine is the statue on your farm.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.43[/b][/size]

[b]The Difficulty setting reaches Hard and Extreme again, Marlon stops selling back last loop's items, and Cactus Fruit waits for the desert.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]The Difficulty setting can reach Hard and Extreme.[/b] Moving the mouse over the list counted as picking, so the page redrew the moment the list opened and only Easy and Normal could ever be chosen. It now waits for your click, and the page stays where you were instead of jumping back to the top. Reported by goblinslayer66666.
[*][b]Marlon no longer sells back last loop's items.[/b] The rewind never cleared the list of things you dropped when you passed out, so the Adventurer's Guild could hand back an item from a previous loop. The rewind now empties it. Reported by Mycatisinapiano1528.
[*][b]Cactus Fruit waits for the desert.[/b] It could land on a board as a crop from Spring, because Cactus Seeds were missing from the list of seeds that wait for Sandy's shop. It now shows up from Fall, like the desert's other forage, or from mid-Summer on Hard. Reported by Mycatisinapiano1528.
[*][b]Four config labels no longer run under their controls.[/b] They are now Better Start gift every loop, Replay mod unlock cutscenes, Gear slots in Gil's Trophies, and Item rarity (TLY Custom only). The tooltips are unchanged.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.38[/b][/size]

[b]The mine's coal carts and barrels come back every loop.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Mine carts and barrels refill when the year rewinds.[/b] A new year in Stardew refills the coal carts and resets the barrels and crates in the mines, but a rewind never counted as a new year, so once you had emptied them they stayed empty for every loop after. The rewind now refills them the way a new year does. Treasure chests still only open once. Contributed by supercam19.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.37[/b][/size]

[b]A season you had finished could still fail, dried fruit and smoked fish now name what they want, and Sneak Peek moves to Wednesday.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Sneak Peek airs on Wednesday.[/b] It used to air next year's episode on Sunday and quietly teach you that week's own recipe alongside it, so the television named one dish and gave you two. It now takes over Wednesday's rerun and shows next year's version of the episode that aired on Sunday, so the two are separate and you can see which one you are getting. You give up the reruns for the season you buy it in. Winter 28's episode has no Wednesday after it, so Shrimp Cocktail is no longer asked for by any bundle.
[*][b]A season you had finished could still fail.[/b] A bundle can only hold as many items as it has slots, but a season's goal could ask for more than that. The bundle went green, the goal still counted you short, and the season failed with nothing you could do about it. Boards from other bundle mods were hit hardest, because a bundle there can share a vanilla bundle's name while having fewer slots. A save already in progress repairs itself the next time you load it. Reported by ozzy2540.
[*][b]Dried fruit and smoked fish now name the fruit and the fish.[/b] These slots only read "Dried" or "Smoked", and nothing in game would tell you which one was wanted, not even Lookup Anything. A dried fruit slot now asks for a named fruit, Dried Apples for instance, and takes only that one. Smoked fish works the same way. Dried mushrooms still take any mushroom, and now say "Any Dried Mushrooms" instead of just "Dried". Reported by ShadowedAciexox.
[*][b]The dried and smoked asks come down.[/b] A dehydrator eats five fruit or five mushrooms for every dried one it makes, which the old numbers never counted, so a slot could ask for thirteen dried mushrooms and mean sixty-five mushrooms. These asks are now sized by what you have to gather rather than by how fast the machines run.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.28[/b][/size]

[b]The Cookbook and Craftbook come with four free slots, a fourth tier takes them to 20, and the bundles can no longer ask for anything a year cannot reach.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Cookbook and Craftbook start with four free slots.[/b] Each book used to start empty until you bought its first tier. Now both hold four recipes from day one, each tier adds four (8, 12, 16), and a new fourth tier at 1200 JP takes them to 20. The first three tiers cost what they did. If your book already holds more than its new limit, every recipe stays banked and usable; the book only refuses new entries until you are back under the limit.
[*][b]Dye and the other pools cannot ask for what a year cannot reach.[/b] The Dye bundle asked for the Queen of Sauce Cookbook, which needs 100 golden walnuts. The colour pools behind Dye, and the pools behind the gem, resource, egg, milk, artifact, mineral, artisan and monster loot asks, now drop anything the mod cannot place inside a year, instead of one item being banned at a time. Reported by SilviaVA.
[*][b]A second visit to a festival lets you leave.[/b] Going back into the Flower Dance on the same day left you stuck: the dance only runs once a day, and that clearing has no way out. When a festival's main event has already happened, the host now offers to let you leave instead. Reported by asteriaths.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.16[/b][/size]

[b]Once-per-loop items always ask for one, and the mine and monster asks now follow what the mines really give.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Once-per-loop items ask for one, as a setting.[/b] Some items a loop can only give once: the five legendary fish, the two books hidden around town and the Golden Pumpkin from the Spirit's Eve maze. The Stack size dial used to turn their ask into two on Hard and Extreme, which no one can ever fill. A new Difficulty setting, on by default, holds every one of them at one whatever the dial says; off, they scale like everything else. A board already asking for two is lowered on load. Thanks to FayGabi for the report.
[*][b]Mine and monster asks follow measured yields.[/b] Every mine floor from 1 to 120 and the first 40 Skull Cavern floors were generated on seven different days, every stone broken, every geode cracked and every monster killed through the game's own drop code, and the result counted. The ore, geode and crystal numbers behind the asks were already right. Four were not: Coal asks go up, since a week of mining gives three to four times what the old number said, Quartz asks come down by more than half, and Topaz, Jade, Aquamarine, Emerald and Ruby asks come down by about half. Drops that only one uncommon monster gives (Squid Ink, Crab Cakes, Cloth, Refined Quartz, the bars, the algae) are now capped at twice what clearing floors actually yields, instead of assuming a whole week spent hunting that one monster.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.11[/b][/size]

[b]The two hidden books are gated fairly: Easy never asks for them, and everyone else gets Fall and Winter to find them.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]The two hidden books get the time their routes take.[/b] Both of the books hidden around town take real work to reach, so their bundle deadlines now sit in Fall and Winter rather than Spring, and on Easy the Book bundle never asks for them at all.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.10[/b][/size]

[b]Five fixes from your reports: festival contests stop the clock, rings stay off the Dye bundle, a new farm survives a quit before its first night, and the Junimo stash works with Chests Anywhere.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Festival contests and cutscenes stop the clock.[/b] The ice fishing contest and the Egg Hunt run on their own real-time timer, and the Flower Dance, the Luau soup and the grange judging take the controls away. The in-game clock kept running through all of them, so the festival's end could pull you out in the middle of the ice fishing contest and leave you stuck holding the contest rod. Time now only passes while you are walking around the festival, and the end of the festival waits until any contest or scene is over. Reported by amaliekirstine.
[*][b]Rings stay off the Dye bundle, and a ring a bundle does ask for can be donated.[/b] The game tags the Amethyst Ring purple, so the Dye bundle could ask for it, and the donation menu then refused to pick it up because a ring is not an ordinary item. Rings are kept out of the colour bundles now, a ring on a board you already have can be picked up and donated, and Hard never asks for two of a ring. The setting called Allow donating tools and rings only ever controlled whether Gil's Trophies asks for a weapon or a hat, so it is now called Weapon and hat slots in Gil's Trophies and says what off does. Reported by FayGabi.
[*][b]Friendship 101 is no longer in the Book bundle.[/b] It is the ninth prize from the prize ticket machine, about 25 Help Wanted quests, and the ticket count starts over every loop, so no one reaches it inside a year. On Hard the Book bundle wants four of its five books, so that one book made the season unwinnable. The Alleyway Buffet and Mapping Cave Systems stay: those books are actually hidden around town, and can be grabbed each loop under the right conditions. Reported by FayGabi.
[*][b]A new farm quit before its first night is still a Longest Year run.[/b] The game saves a brand-new farm the moment you finish making your character, before this mod has written anything to it. Quitting on that first Spring 1 without sleeping and reloading gave you a farm with no books, no shrine, no Junimo chest and a locked Community Center. The run is now marked in that first save, and a farm you already have in that state is picked up as a run the next time you load it. Reported by FayGabi.
[*][b]The Junimo stash works with Chests Anywhere.[/b] You can name it, give it a category, and switch to another chest from it. The stash was opened in a way that hid it from Chests Anywhere, to keep Better Chests and Unlimited Storage from resizing it; that now only happens when one of those two mods is installed, and in that case the stash is simply left out of the Chests Anywhere list so you can never get stuck in it. Reported by asteriaths and FayGabi.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.4[/b][/size]

[b]One Difficulty setting for all ten dials, and two fixes from your reports.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]One Difficulty setting sets all ten dials.[/b] A new Difficulty option sits at the top of the Difficulty section. Pick Easy, Normal, Hard or Extreme and every dial below it switches to that level, then change any single dial you like. Normal is the default, and a setup you already have is left as it is.
[*][b]Gil's Trophies never asks for more than one of a trophy.[/b] On Hard and Extreme the Stack size dial was raising a trophy to two, but Gil gives each one only once and hats, the Insect Head and rings never stack, so that slot could never be filled. Every trophy now asks for one, and a board that already has a two on it is fixed the next time you load the save. Reported by ShadowedAciexox.
[*][b]Quitting after a failed season's last night no longer skips the rewind.[/b] Going to bed on day 28 saves the game already dated to the next season, and the rewind only happened the next morning. Quitting before it played and then reloading carried the run into a season you had not earned. The save now remembers the rewind is owed, and reloading plays it. Reported by gmastern1.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.1[/b][/size]

[b]Garlic can be cultivated too, and both Cultivation upgrades are cheaper.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Cultivation: Garlic joins the upgrade menu, and both Cultivation upgrades drop to 3,000 Junimo Points.[/b] The upgrade menu sold Cultivation: Red Cabbage and nothing for Garlic, which was backwards: Red Cabbage turns up at the Traveling Cart in year 1, while Garlic has no year-1 source at all. Garlic now has the same deal, a 10% chance from Spring Mixed Seeds, and both cost 3,000 instead of Red Cabbage's old 5,000. Buying both is still cheaper than Pierre's Special Order, which stays the guaranteed route. Raised by Tottelotta123.
[*][b]Artichoke is no longer held off an Easy board.[/b] On the Easy item-rarity setting all three of Pierre's year-two crops were kept off the board until you bought an upgrade, but Artichoke never needed one: Mixed Seeds planted in Fall give Artichoke Seeds about a quarter of the time, in any year, for free.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.18.0[/b][/size]

[b]The Mod Compatibility Update: bundles no longer ask for things this run cannot reach, and a board that already has one gets repaired.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Bundles no longer ask for things this run cannot reach.[/b] Reported by pitytheviolins: with The Fishmonger installed, a Community Center bundle asked for a dish only Constance sells, from a shop on Ginger Island, which this mod's time loop never reaches. There was no way to complete that bundle. The game now traces every item back to where it actually comes from (a shop, a crop's seed, a cooking recipe) and keeps an item off the board unless at least one of those routes is somewhere this run can reach. An item with no known source at all is left alone, so this only ever removes things proven unreachable, never guesses.
[*][b]A board you already have gets repaired, not just new ones.[/b] If a bundle on your current board is asking for something this run can never reach, it is swapped for something you can actually get the next time you load that save. Anything you already donated stays donated.
[*][b]The Abandoned Joja Mart's bundle is vanilla again.[/b] The Missing Bundle was being re-rolled by the mod's own board generator, which is how it came to ask for a legendary fish. That room sits outside the loop entirely, so it is now passed through untouched exactly as the Vault always has been, and a save that already picked up a re-rolled version gets the real one back on its next rewind. Reported by ChaoticMindset.
[*][b]Zoom Level and UI Scale survive the rewind.[/b] Both dials snapped back to the game's defaults every time the Junimos rewound the year, and there was no way to change what those defaults were. The game treats them as belonging to the save rather than to you, so the fresh year was starting them over while every other setting came back on its own. The loop now carries both across the reset. Reported by RiseiJaku.
[/list]

Coming from 0.17.15 or earlier? See the previous update below, or the full history in [url=https://github.com/sonofskywalker3/TheLongestYear/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url].

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.17.12[/b][/size]

[b]The Reasonable Quantities Update: every ask on the board is now a share of what you can really gather, and the difficulty dials finally mean what they say.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Every bundle asks for a share of what a week of going after it actually yields.[/b] Fish, forage, crops, crab pots, monster drops, the mines, animals, machines and raw resources each have a real weekly yield behind them now: fish modelled from the game's own spawn tables at a level-10 fishing pace, forage measured by sweeping every map for three in-game years, crops on 100 tiles, ten crab pots, a full day in the mines. Your Stack size dial then picks a share of it: Easy 10 to 30%, Normal 20 to 50%, Hard 50 to 65%, Extreme 65 to 80%, never above 80%. Two Smallmouth Bass is no longer an Extreme ask, and 90 Common Mushrooms is no longer a Spring one.
[*][b]Legendary fish are asked for once, plain, and rarely.[/b] Never two of one, never at silver or gold. A Normal board wants at most one legendary and only one board in four wants any; Hard boards up to two, Extreme up to three, and never two from the same season in one bundle. The Hard and Extreme dial used to double a single legendary into an impossible pair.
[*][b]Hard and Extreme mean it.[/b] Before, the Stack size dial multiplied a one-item ask into two, so Hard and Extreme were identical for most of the board. Now an Extreme Spring Foraging bundle wants 40 to 60 of each item, an Extreme Adventurer's 80 Slimes, an Extreme Jeweler's a dozen of each gem.
[*][b]Two new mineral bundles.[/b] Jeweler's (the seven fancy gems, a Diamond for finishing it) and Rockhound's (geode minerals, a Geode Crusher) join Mineral in the Boiler Room, and all three now ask for rocks only rather than the artifacts geodes also drop.
[*][b]0.17.12: the Copper Pan and chained scenes come back every loop.[/b] Same family: Willy's pan scene, and any scene that only unlocks after another scene that replays (the 14-heart chains, Shane's morning-after, Pam's bus follow-up), were stuck as seen from loop 1.
[*][b]0.17.12: Willy's letter arrives after you keep playing.[/b] A finished Community Center could still be read as unfinished by the mod's own check, which silently blocked the game from sending Willy's back-room letter, so Ginger Island stayed shut. The restored hall is now the authority. Reported by ChaoticMindset.
[*][b]0.17.12: quest-finishing scenes play again every loop.[/b] Jodi's fish casserole dinner and Marnie's cave carrot thank-you were being treated as already seen from your first loop, so the quest came back each loop but could never be turned in. Reported by ChaoticMindset.
[*][b]0.17.12: Gunther brings the Rusty Key again every loop.[/b] The museum empties on the rewind and the 60-donation reward re-fired, but Gunther's farm visit that hands the key over never played again, so the sewers stayed shut after loop 1 unless you had bought the keep. Reported by ChaoticMindset.
[*][b]0.17.8: a must-donate-all bundle's season gate takes any of its items.[/b] The Bundle Log showed only the items pinned to the current season and the gate refused the rest. The pins now decide how many are due; which ones you bring is your call. Reported by ada113.
[*][b]0.17.8: the Cookbook and Craftbook open between the upgrade menu and the reset.[/b] A book bought in the upgrade menu had nothing to bank by the time it first opened, because the reset had already wiped your recipes. Each book with a free slot now opens right after the upgrade menu. Reported by ada113.
[*][b]0.17.6: a crops bundle every season.[/b] The Pantry always has Spring Crops, Summer Crops and Fall Crops on the board now. A board could roll Orchard, Preserver's and Home Cook's Feast in their place, which left the Farming theme with nothing to ask for in week 1 but saplings.
[*][b]0.17.6: one jelly a week.[/b] A weekly theme asks for at most one of Sea Jelly, River Jelly and Cave Jelly. Two of them in the same week meant two slow, separate fishing trips for one theme.
[*][b]0.17.5: every farm type.[/b] Riverland, Forest, Hilltop, Wilderness, Four Corners, Beach and Meadowlands are all open now; the mod no longer forces Standard. Kept buildings go back to your own spots and the Junimo stash sits by your door on any map. Balance is shared across types, see Limitations.
[*][b]0.17.5: the Skip intro checkbox is back.[/b] Rerolling farms? Tick Skip intro on the character screen and the opening scene is skipped, straight to the theme picker. A note pops up recommending you watch it the first time, since it is the only in-game explanation of the loop. Asked for by gazumbrado.
[*][b]0.17.5: new book art.[/b] The Cookbook, Craftbook and Bundle Log have proper covers now, drawn by [b]supercam19[/b]. Thank you!
[*][b]0.17.1: the Dye bundle never asks for a legendary fish.[/b] It picks by colour, and a green Legend or a red Crimsonfish counted. Its season gates were already right.
[*][b]Fixes from your reports.[/b] Golden Egg (Perfection only) and Son of Crimsonfish (a Mr. Qi quest) can no longer be asked for. A Spring bundle can no longer want 90 Common Mushrooms because Fall Wild Seeds could theoretically grow them. Coffee Bean, Cloth and a few Skull Cavern drops were asking for more than a first loop can produce. Normal now caps a vanilla ask at a stack, so Hard never asks for fewer than Normal.
[*][b]Thank you to gazumbrado, nyxnyx2234, spenderg and Bumblewyn[/b] for the reports and the reroll logs behind this release.
[/list]

Coming from 0.15.0 or earlier? 0.16.0 added ten independent [b]Difficulty[/b] dials in the settings menu and made every bundle apply pressure at the season checkpoints, which makes the year harder at every difficulty. Details in [url=https://github.com/sonofskywalker3/TheLongestYear/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url].

[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Seasonal time-loop.[/b] Each season has a donation minimum. Miss it and the year unwinds to Spring 1.
[*][b]Junimo Points.[/b] Donations earn JP — scaled by rarity and by how late in the year you give. JP banks across loops.
[*][b]Junimo Upgrades.[/b] Spend JP on upgrades that let you hold on to some of what you gained: skill levels, tool tiers, recipes, buildings, a kept pet, the power books you have read, your wallet items and Stardrops, the Junimos' own gifts (greenhouse, quarry bridge, boulder, minecarts, bus), and more.
[*][b]JP Boosts.[/b] The Junimo statue on your farm sells this-loop edges for JP: tomorrow's rain or a lucky day, a free late night, stacking forage/fish/crop/mine/drop chances, a faster walk, a season of cheaper shops, faster friendships, extra energy, a skill level on the spot, or an elevator stop you have not earned yet. An Active tab shows what is running and a Plan tab shows what each keep still needs.
[*][b]Weekly themes.[/b] Each week, pick one of two themes (Foraging, Farming, Fishing, Mining, Mixed, Spelunking, Artisan, Kitchen) for a bonus and a paired liability. Goals follow the season gate and the weekly bonus is paid per goal.
[*][b]Carryover surfaces.[/b] A [b]Bundle Log[/b] book that tracks each season's goals, a Cookbook and Craftbook to bank recipes, a [b]Herd Book[/b] that brings your registered animals back with their hearts, and a Junimo Stash chest that survives resets.
[*][b]A real intro.[/b] Lewis greets you on the porch; a Junimo explains the loop. Then the run begins.
[*][b]A starved Traveling Cart.[/b] Joja has squeezed the merchant's suppliers — the cart carries [b]one item[/b] per visit until you unlock more stalls with the [b]Cart Stall[/b] upgrades (and Cart Whisperer previews what's coming). Prefer the full vanilla cart? Turn off [font=Courier New]LimitTravelingCartStock[/font].
[*][b]The town half-remembers.[/b] Villagers you have spent a lot of time with across loops occasionally say something uncanny. Rare, no gameplay effect, and it never explains itself. Toggle in Features.
[*][b]Break the loop.[/b] Finish the Center in a year to win — then keep playing or start fresh.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Stardew Valley 1.6+[/b] (PC: Windows, Linux, macOS)
[*][b]SMAPI 4.0.0[/b] or newer
[*]A [b]new save[/b] (any farm type; see the note under Limitations)
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://smapi.io/]SMAPI[/url] (4.0.0+).
[*]Download the latest [font=Courier New]TheLongestYear[/font] release and unzip it into your [font=Courier New]Stardew Valley/Mods[/font] folder, so you have [font=Courier New]Mods/TheLongestYear/TheLongestYear.dll[/font].
[*]Launch the game through SMAPI.
[*][b]Start a new game[/b] on any farm type. Leave [b]Skip intro[/b] off the first time: the mod's own opening plays in place of the vanilla one and explains the loop. Tick it on later farms to go straight to the theme picker.
[*][b]Community Center Bundles[/b] under [b]New → Advanced Options[/b] defaults to [b]TLY Custom[/b]: every loop rolls a fresh board from the vanilla + remix pools plus the mod's own authored bundles. Prefer the game's own board (or another bundle mod's)? Pick [b]Normal[/b] or [b]Remixed[/b] there instead — the mod keeps that board and re-rolls it the same way on every reset. (You can change this later: [font=Courier New]Bundle source[/font] in GMCM switches an existing save between all three, applying at its next loop.)
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1303/images/47192/47192-1787355673-935410882.png[/img]
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The intro.[/b] On a fresh game, Lewis greets you on the porch, then a Junimo explains the loop. You wake on Spring 1 and pick your first [b]weekly theme[/b].
[*][b]Weekly themes.[/b] Each week you choose one of two offered themes. Room themes (Foraging, Farming, Fishing, Mining) take goals from their Community Center room; Spelunking, Artisan and Kitchen take goals by item kind from anywhere on the board, and Mixed takes anything. Goals follow what the season gate demands first; the weekly JP bonus is paid goal by goal and the drawback lifts when every goal is done. The planning hub opens at the start of each week.
[*][b]Seasonal goals.[/b] The [b]Bundle Log[/b] book (click to open) tracks each season's required donations. Each season has a minimum you must donate to the Center before the season turns. [b]Miss it and the year unwinds to Spring 1.[/b]
[*][b]Fail night.[/b] When a season's minimum is missed, the Junimos rewind the year. Before the upgrade menu opens, they ask whether to keep the same bundle board for the next loop or let time reshuffle it. The first hold is free; each further hold in a row costs 50, 100, 200, then 300 JP, and reshuffling resets the price. This works on every bundle source.
[*][b]Junimo Points (JP).[/b] Donations earn JP, scaled by rarity and by how late in the year you give (later seasons are worth much more). JP banks across loops.
[*][b]Junimo Upgrades.[/b] On every loop reset (and on a win), spend banked JP on upgrades that let you [i]hold on to some of what you gained[/i] next loop — skill levels, tool tiers, recipes, buildings, a kept pet, the power books you have read, your wallet items and Stardrops, and more.
[*][b]JP Boosts.[/b] The Junimo statue on the farm sells this-loop edges for JP any day (weather, luck, a free late night, stacking bonuses, a temporary skill level, an elevator stop) and shows what is running on its Active tab.
[*][b]Carryover surfaces on the farm.[/b] A [b]Cookbook[/b] (kitchen) and [b]Craftbook[/b] (table) let you bank recipes to keep; a [b]Junimo Stash[/b] chest preserves a few items across resets.
[*][b]Restarting.[/b] Want a fresh loop before the season runs out? The Junimo Shrine's [b]Restart the year[/b] button ends the day and runs a Fail night without the Junimo scene: keep or reshuffle your bundles, spend JP, bank recipes, and wake on Spring 1. It counts as a loop, and it works after Keep playing too.
[*][b]Winning.[/b] Restore the entire Community Center within a year to break the loop. You can then choose to keep playing that run or start a fresh loop.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Difficulty[/b][/size]
Nine difficulty dials live in the mod's settings menu (GMCM) under [b]Difficulty[/b], with one overall [b]Difficulty[/b] option above them. Pick a level there and every dial switches to it, then change any single dial you like. Every dial has four steps, [b]Easy / Normal / Hard / Extreme[/b], and every one starts on [b]Normal[/b], which is the balance the mod ships with. Changing nothing changes nothing.

[b]Changes take effect on your next loop, not straight away.[/b] The dials are stamped onto your save when a loop begins, so the year you are already playing keeps the rules it started under.
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1303/images/47192/47192-1787870999-2094236733.png[/img]

[b]What the bundles ask for[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Stack size.[/b] How many of an item a slot asks for, as a share of what a week of going after it actually yields: Easy 10 to 30%, Normal 20 to 50%, Hard 50 to 65%, Extreme 65 to 80%, and never above 80%. Fish, forage, crops, crab pots, monster drops, the mines, animals and machines each have their own yield behind that number, and a yield is capped at one stack of 99 (Slime, Bat Wings and the like), so an Extreme ask of 80 is a stack, not a share. Artifacts stay at one. Money bundles are never affected.
[*][b]Once-per-loop items ask for one.[/b] On by default. The five legendary fish, the two books hidden around town and the Golden Pumpkin can only be had once in a loop, so a bundle never asks for more than one of them whatever Stack size says. Off, they scale like everything else. Takes effect at the next reset.
[*][b]Quality asks.[/b] How often a slot wants a silver or gold star. Items the game never gives a star to are still never asked for at quality, at any step.
[*][b]Required slots.[/b] How many of a bundle's shown items you must actually donate. Hard asks for one more, Easy one fewer, Extreme asks for all of them.
[*][b]Item rarity.[/b] Weights bundles toward harder items: rarer, later in the year, or needing a keg or a press. [b]TLY Custom bundles only[/b] (see below).
[/list]

[b]What you carry between loops[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Junimo Points earned.[/b] Scales every JP award, so progress across loops is faster or slower. The season ramp keeps its shape, so late-season donating is still worth the most.
[*][b]Upgrade prices.[/b] Scales what upgrades cost in the upgrade menu.
[*][b]Starting gold.[/b] Scales the [font=Courier New]StartingMoney[/font] value rather than replacing it. Extreme starts you with nothing.
[*][b]Starting cart slots.[/b] How many items the Traveling Cart offers before you buy any Cart Stall upgrade. On Hard and Extreme the cart is empty until you buy Cart Stall I.
[*][b]Hold prices.[/b] Scales the JP price of keeping your board on a Fail night. The first hold stays free at every step.
[/list]

[b]One dial does not work on vanilla boards.[/b] Item rarity applies to [b]TLY Custom[/b] bundles only, because changing which item a vanilla bundle asks for would be changing the bundle. Stack size, quality asks and required slots all work on vanilla Standard and Remixed boards too.

[font=Courier New]tly_difficulty[/font] in the SMAPI console prints what your save is actually running under, including anything you have changed since your last loop. Please attach it to any balance report.

[line]

[size=5][b]Switching bundle source later[/b][/size]
You are not locked into the board you picked when you started. [b]Bundle source[/b] in the mod's settings menu (GMCM) is one setting with three choices, and you can move an existing save between any of them:
[list]
[*][b]TLY Custom[/b] - the mod composes a fresh board every loop from the vanilla and remix pools plus its own authored bundles.
[*][b]Normal[/b] - the game's own standard bundle layout, re-rolled the same way each loop.
[*][b]Remixed[/b] - the game's own remixed layout, likewise.
[/list]

Another bundle mod's board is covered by Normal or Remixed: whatever the game generates is what the mod keeps.

Like the difficulty dials, a switch applies at your [b]next loop[/b], not straight away. The year you are already playing keeps the board it started with.

[b]Keeping your board on a Fail night works on all three.[/b] If you hold, you get the same board back next loop whichever source it came from.

[line]

[size=5][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
The [b]Features[/b] section of the settings menu turns individual parts of the mod off or tunes them, and changes there apply straight away:
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1303/images/47192/47192-1787870999-1916723524.png[/img]
All knobs live in [font=Courier New]Mods/TheLongestYear/config.json[/font] (created on first run). The values most worth tuning during the beta:
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Jp.CommonJp[/font] / [font=Courier New]UncommonJp[/font] / [font=Courier New]RareJp[/font] / [font=Courier New]VeryRareJp[/font] (default 1 / 3 / 10 / 25): JP awarded per donated item by rarity
[*][font=Courier New]Jp.SeasonMultipliers[/font] (default [font=Courier New][1.0, 1.5, 2.5, 4.0][/font]): Per-season JP multiplier (Spring→Winter)
[*][font=Courier New]Jp.BundleCompletionBonus[/font] / [font=Courier New]RoomCompletionBonus[/font] / [font=Courier New]WeeklyQuestCompletionBonus[/font] (default 15 / 60 / 30): Bonus JP for milestones (×season multiplier)
[*][font=Courier New]StartingMoney[/font] (default 500): Gold at the start of each loop
[*][font=Courier New]BundleQuotas[/font] (default per-bundle): How much each percentage-bundle asks for
[*][font=Courier New]StashTileX/Y[/font] (default [font=Courier New]0,0[/font], auto): Where the Junimo Stash chest is placed ([font=Courier New]0,0[/font] = auto-pick near the farmhouse). The Bundle Log / Cookbook / Craftbook are placeable furniture you can put anywhere.
[*][font=Courier New]LimitTravelingCartStock[/font] (default [font=Courier New]true[/font]): Cap the Traveling Cart to the stalls unlocked by the Cart Stall upgrades (one item until Cart Stall II). [font=Courier New]false[/font] = full vanilla cart
[*][font=Courier New]BundleSource[/font] (default [font=Courier New]Engine[/font]): One setting, three values: [font=Courier New]Engine[/font] (the mod's own board every loop, the new-game [b]TLY Custom[/b] choice), [font=Courier New]Normal[/font] or [font=Courier New]Remixed[/font] (the game's own board of that kind, or another bundle mod's, re-rolled the same way each loop). Switchable on an existing save; takes effect at the next loop. See Switching bundle source later
[*][font=Courier New]BundleHoldCosts[/font] (default [font=Courier New][0, 50, 100, 200, 300][/font]): JP cost of keeping the same bundle board on a Fail night, by how many holds you have taken in a row (first is free; the last value repeats). Reshuffling resets the count
[*][font=Courier New]Enabled[/font] (default [font=Courier New]true[/font]): Master switch: turn the whole mod off to play vanilla
[/list]
Upgrade prices are defined in the upgrade catalog (e.g. Cookbook/Craftbook tiers at 150 / 350 / 700 / 1200 JP). Feedback on these is welcome.

[line]

[size=5][b]Is this a bug?[/b][/size]

A few things get reported often enough to be worth answering up front.

[b]Demetrius never shows up about the cave, I just get a popup asking mushrooms or bats.[/b]
That is the mod, working as intended. His scene plays once per playthrough; from the second loop on, walking into the farm cave gives you the choice directly instead of replaying a cutscene you have already watched. The mushrooms-or-bats decision is re-offered every loop because the rewind clears it.

[b]The Traveling Cart only has one item.[/b]
Also intended. Joja is squeezing the merchant's suppliers, and the Cart Stall upgrades in the upgrade menu add slots back. If you would rather have the full cart, turn off LimitTravelingCartStock in the config.

[b]I did the Egg Hunt and now Lewis will not let me do it again today.[/b]
Since 0.14.1, a festival's main event runs once per day. Festivals in this mod do not end your day, so you can walk out and back in - which used to restart the whole festival and let the hunt be repeated for the prize. The stalls, the shop and everyone at the festival still work on a repeat visit. A new loop is a clean slate: as far as the valley is concerned the festival has not happened yet, so you get to do it again.

[b]A bundle is asking for silver or gold on something that cannot have a quality.[/b]
That was a bug and it is fixed. Quality is only ever asked for on things the game itself gives quality to (crop harvests, rod-caught fish, spawned forage). Existing boards pick the change up at the next reset.

[b]A weekly goal ticked off without me donating anything.[/b]
Fixed in 0.14.0. Finishing a bundle that only needs some of its listed items used to mark the rest as filled, which credited goals you never handed in. A goal now waits for the real donation.

[b]I bought Keep Bus Unlocked and the Vault bundles are still on the board.[/b]
Intended. The gift keeps the bus and the desert open from day 1; the Vault bundles are still part of restoring the Center, still have to be paid, and still earn JP. Completing them again does not replay the repair scene. Every Gift of the Junimos works this way.

[b]The skill level I bought at the statue was gone after the rewind.[/b]
Intended. Crash Course levels are temporary: they last the loop, never reach level 10, and cannot be kept. Only levels you earn open the Keep Level rows on a Fail night.

[b]Elevator Pass says "Enter the mine first", or a weather boost says "Not now".[/b]
Both intended. The pass extends the elevator from wherever it already reaches, so it needs one trip into the mine first. Rain Dance and Storm Call are refused on day 28 and the day before a festival, because the game forces sunshine on those mornings and the JP would be wasted.

[b]My enchanted sword lost its enchantments in the Junimo Stash.[/b]
Fixed since 0.16.7. Tools and weapons in the stash keep their enchantments, forged gems, bait and tackle across the rewind.

Anything not on this list, please do report - the bugs tab on Nexus is read.

[line]

[size=5][b]Limitations (beta)[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]PC only.[/b] No Android port yet.
[*][b]Farm types are balanced as a set, not individually.[/b] The bundle asks are sized from Standard farm yields. Each other type trades one thing for another (Riverland and Beach: more fish, less field; Forest: more forage; Hilltop: more ore; Wilderness: more monsters; Meadowlands: easier animals), so the year is a little easier in some bundles and a little harder in others. Beach farm's no-sprinklers rule makes its crop bundles a real step harder. Custom farm maps that replace a vanilla slot load fine but are untested for balance.
[*][b]Start on a new save.[/b] A run can only begin from a new game; other saves load normally and are left untouched.
[*]Intro cutscene and dialogue are a first pass.
[*]Multiplayer is untested.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Giving feedback[/b][/size]
What helps most right now:
[list=1]
[*][b]Difficulty[/b]: do the seasonal minimums feel fair? Too punishing, too easy? Which season wall hit hardest?
[*][b]Pricing[/b]: are JP earnings and upgrade costs well-balanced? What did you save for first, and did it feel worth it?
[*][b]Pacing[/b]: how many loops before the run "clicked"? Did the carryover make later loops feel meaningfully stronger?
[*][b]Bugs / crashes[/b]: include your [font=Courier New]SMAPI-latest.txt[/font] ([font=Courier New]Stardew Valley/ErrorLogs/[/font]).
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Art wanted[/b][/size]
The mod leans on vanilla sprites for most things. If anyone would enjoy making some custom [b]sprite artwork[/b] (the shrine, the stash chest, icons), I'd genuinely love to accept it and credit you. Drop a note in the comments.

[i]Banner art by [b]cwybabiesucks[/b]. Book art by [b]supercam19[/b]. Thank you both![/i]

[line]

[size=5][b]Translations[/b][/size]
As of 0.11.60, every player-visible string in the mod lives in a JSON file ([font=Courier New]i18n/default.json[/font]) — the mod is fully translatable with no DLL edits or rebuilds. See [url=https://github.com/sonofskywalker3/TheLongestYear/blob/master/docs/TRANSLATING.md]TRANSLATING.md[/url] for how to add a language. If you translate it, let us know (Nexus DM or GitHub issue) and we'll link your work from the mod page.

